    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="1067" n="873" xml:id="pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley Files</note>
                <head>No. 929<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d929-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: The other day I gave you
                    very briefly a verbal statement concerning several observations by my staff of
                    machine tool shipments from the Berlin area.</p>
                <p>I am sending herewith a copy of the report turned in to me by Dr. Luther Gulick,
                    and J. Howard Marshall, the General Counsel of our Delegation.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin W. Pauley</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d929-a1.xml" xpointer="d929-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
